    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0814" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4308: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-26T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 26—9:28
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>172. Seventh paragraph my 164 of April 24. Admiral Strauss<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d436-f1"/> sailed from Manila yesterday on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Huron</hi> for Chinwangtao. U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Albany</hi> is
                    expected at same port tomorrow noon bringing 175 officers and men to reinforce
                    Legation Guard. This will bring strength of guard up to 525.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d436-f1" n="28" xml:id="d436-f1-content">
                <p>Rear Admiral Joseph Strauss, Commander in Chief, U. S. Asiatic Fleet.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
